// AC timer (sleep / scheduled on / scheduled off)
//
// `actm` has ASYMMETRIC encoding between the wire and status:
//   * On the wire (control publish): two-element array of RELATIVE
//     durations in seconds — how many seconds from now the timer
//     should fire. -1 means "no timer for this slot" (CLEARS any
//     existing timer in that slot, does NOT preserve it).
//   * In status replies: same field, but the broker has already
//     added its current `ts` to produce absolute Unix timestamps
//     in seconds.
//
// Slot order is [off_timer, on_timer] in both directions. Both
// slots are sent on every update — to preserve an existing timer
// in the other slot while modifying one, the caller must compute
// its remaining seconds-until-fire and re-send that.
//
// Example: schedule the AC to turn off in 1 hour, no on-timer.
{
    "actm": [3600, -1],
    "ki": 1,
    "cnt": "an",
    "sid": "0"
}
